thermal: add a driver for the Sophgo CV18xx TEMPSEN block

The CV18xx/SG200x SoCs have an on-chip temperature sensor (TEMPSEN,
0x030e0000, clocked by CLK_TEMPSEN off the 25 MHz oscillator). There
is no mainline driver for it (checked up to 7.2-rc), so this is a new,
minimal driver written against the 6.12 thermal API. The register
programming (acquisition setup, DDR refresh-rate threshold defaults
and the result-to-millicelsius formula, T[mC] = raw * 716000 / 2048 -
273000) is taken from the vendor 5.10 cv181x_thermal.c, which this
driver replaces functionally; the vendor's thermal_zone_of_sensor API
and per-channel boilerplate are gone, and only channel 0 -- the only
one the vendor driver ever read -- is exposed, via
devm_thermal_of_zone_register().

The sensor free-runs one measurement about every 2 s once enabled;
get_temp() just reads the latest CH0 result. A zero result (only seen
before the first conversion completes) returns -EAGAIN rather than
being converted to -273 degC. Like the vendor kernel, the driver also
programs the DDR high/low temperature thresholds and enables the
block's DDR auto-refresh-rate control output.

Signed-off-by: d622 <300083818+d622-au@users.noreply.github.com>

